{"title":"Specific Needs (2)","puid":"c-sci-3-gb/j5olfz","path":"/../c-sci-3-gb/topic-02-plants/block-01-plants/level-05","type":"normal","keyboardLayout":"standardNATENG","voiceLang":"en","voice":"m2_2025","instruction":{"voice":"f3_2025","speaker":true},"trainers":[{"trainer":"gap","gapMode":"buttons","instruction":{"text":"Fill in the gaps."},"image":{"image":"bigstockphoto_250954078","width":200},"textAlign":"left","shuffleButtons":true,"soundMode":"b","atoms":{"b":"Palms are ((tropical --underwater)) plants. This means they grow well in places with lots of ((sunlight --nutrients)) and ((warm --cool)) temperatures. The <b>tropics</b> provide palms with plenty of ((water --wind)) and ((moisture --dryness)), however palms grow best in ((sand --clay)) and other types of soil that <b>drain</b> well. Palms are able to grow near ((salt_water --snow)) because their roots can absorb water from the ((ocean --air)) and leave the <b>salt</b> behind."}},{"trainer":"imageButtons","instruction":{"text":"Based on the text, where do palms grow best?"},"onSamePage":true,"shuffleButtons":true,"atoms":{"b":[{"image":{"image":"adobe_71658901","width":150},"correct":true},{"image":{"image":"bigstockphoto_226506451","width":150}}]}},{"trainer":"gap","gapMode":"buttons","image":{"image":"adobe_209196036","width":200},"instruction":{"text":"Fill in the gaps."},"textAlign":"left","shuffleButtons":true,"soundMode":"b","atoms":{"b":"This is a very special plant called a venus ((flytrap --antsnap)). It is a ((carnivorous --nutritious)) plant and can consume living creatures! <b>Flytraps</b> use hairs on the end of their leaves to sense if an ((insect --bird)) has landed on it and then snap the leaf closed to trap it. It then <b>digests</b> the insect and receives important ((nutrients --information)). It is a <b>subtropical</b> plant and, therefore, needs a good amount of ((sunlight --fertiliser)) and ((water --soil)). They also enjoy a high amount of <b>humidity</b>, or ((moisture --oxygen)), in the air."}},{"trainer":"imageButtons","instruction":{"text":"Based on the text, where do venus flytraps grow best?"},"onSamePage":true,"shuffleButtons":true,"atoms":{"b":[{"image":{"image":"adobe_239951335","width":150},"correct":true},{"image":{"image":"bigstockphoto_237312286_crop-530-0-1068-1068","width":150}}]}},{"trainer":"dragAndValidate","instruction":{"text":"Drag the correct plant to its <b>habitat</b>.","speaker":true},"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-3-gb/topic-02-plants/block-01-plants/lsg/habitat3.lsg","width":200},"validateMode":"group","shuffleAtoms":true,"zoneFlow":"center","atoms":[{"b":{"zone":"z2"},"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-3-gb/topic-02-plants/block-01-plants/lsg/palm.lsg","width":130}},{"b":{"zone":""},"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-3-gb/topic-02-plants/block-01-plants/lsg/flytrap.lsg","width":130}}]},{"trainer":"dragAndValidate","instruction":{"text":"Drag the correct plant to its <b>habitat</b>.","speaker":true},"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-3-gb/topic-02-plants/block-01-plants/lsg/habitat2.lsg","width":200},"validateMode":"group","shuffleAtoms":true,"zoneFlow":"center","atoms":[{"b":{"zone":""},"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-3-gb/topic-02-plants/block-01-plants/lsg/palm.lsg","width":130}},{"b":{"zone":"z4"},"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-3-gb/topic-02-plants/block-01-plants/lsg/flytrap.lsg","width":130}}]},{"trainer":"dragAndValidate","instruction":{"text":"Which plants need <b>more sunlight</b> to grow and which ones don’t? Drag the plants to the correct side."},"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-3-gb/topic-02-plants/block-01-plants/lsg/dragsun.lsg","width":400},"validateMode":"group","shuffleAtoms":true,"zoneFlow":"center","atoms":[{"b":{"zone":"z1"},"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-3-gb/topic-02-plants/block-01-plants/lsg/palm.lsg","width":100}},{"b":{"zone":"z1"},"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-3-gb/topic-02-plants/block-01-plants/lsg/flytrap.lsg","width":100}},{"b":{"zone":"z1"},"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-3-gb/topic-02-plants/block-01-plants/lsg/cactus.lsg","width":100}},{"b":{"zone":"z2"},"lsg":{